{
  "name": "scatter_arabic",
  "description": "Arabic consonants as a scatter overlay on the vocal tract. 11 columns (glottal, pharyngeal, uvular, velar, palatal, post-alveolar, alveolar, dental, interdental, labio-dental, bilabial) ordered back→front. 12 rows × 0.1in delta_r centered at r=2.5. 28 cells filled out of 132 (from AP3 audiography source). Arabic's 'spread but sparse' signature is the visible pattern.",
